<title>CHINA: Shanghai to auction Belgian ship.</title>
<headline>Shanghai to auction Belgian ship.</headline>
<dateline>SHANGHAI 1996-11-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Shanghai Maritime Court will auction a Belgian ship on November 25 because the owner failed to pay a $2 million repair bill to a local shipyard, a court official said on Monday.</p>
<p>The 27,071-tonne Norbel Bulk, built in 1973 and owned by the Norbel Shipping Inc in Belgium, will be the biggest of about 20 ships which the Shanghai Maritime Court has auctioned since 1985, the official said.</p>
<p>The court seized the ship on May 29 at the request of the shipyard which wanted payment for repairs, the court said in a notice in the Liberation Daily newspaper.</p>
<p>The official gave no further details.</p>
</text>
